<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25971" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lătĕrīcĭus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-tĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		later, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>made</i> or <i>consisting of bricks</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">turris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. C. 2, 10</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">2, 14</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">muri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">opus,</span>”
				<i>brickwork</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					9, 6, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbs,</span>”
				<i>built of bricks</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 28</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">paries,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					18, 30, 73, § 301</span></i>
			.—Hence, <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lătĕrīcĭum</span></b> ,
				ii, n., <i>brickwork</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ne saxa ex catapultis latericium discuterent,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. C. 2, 9, 4</span></i>
			.</div>
